This is the fifth step toward our process migrating to TypeScript, with an actual refactor to TypeScript.

The `CSSClasses` and `Props` types will be shared across the widget and the component in the future.

### Preact alternative for typing for a functional component

This is an alternative (with which the tests fail). I think the one I went for in the PR is fine.

```js
import { FunctionalComponent } from 'preact';
import React from 'preact-compat';

type CSSClasses = {
  root: string;
  link: string;
  logo: string;
};

type Props = {
  url: string;
  theme: string;
  cssClasses: CSSClasses;
};

const PoweredBy: FunctionalComponent<Props> = ({ url, theme, cssClasses }) => (
  // ...
);
```

[See more →](https://github.com/scurker/preact-and-typescript#example-usage-1)

